# The canonical form writes a very small or very large Float with an
# exponent, which now reads back (S8; before it, `1e-7` did not lex,
# so the formatter's round trip failed for such numbers).
== SOURCE
0.0000001 + 100000000000000000000000.0
== CANONICAL
(1e-7 + 1e23)
== RESULT
100000000000000000000000.0
